From ed96325742eb8b1d7bd0b492a150a4da02377860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:01:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper v1.7.1: security remediation batch (audit 2026-07-21)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Addresses the findings in Reaper_v1.7.0_Security_Audit. All on be96u-only canon;
siblings port later. No critical/high existed; these harden the confirmed items.

M1 (med) CSRF: do_reaper_wifi_cgi now requires http_id on every state-changing
  action (capstart/capstop/scanstart/scanstop/chqset), matching the gk/mcp CGIs;
  Reaper_Wireless.asp sends the token on all 6 mutating calls. Stale "read-only
  toward the radio" header comment corrected (scanstart retunes).
M2 (med) gk_rl lost-update race: gkd expire_guests() now re-reads gk_rl FRESH
  under an flock(/tmp/gk/rl.lock), and httpd gk_rl_update() takes the same lock,
  so an admin approve/block can no longer be clobbered by a concurrent guest
  expiry.
L1 (low) injection: gk_gen_apply validates each MAC with gk_valid_mac() before
  it flows unquoted into the root-run apply.sh (was length-only).
L4 gkd devs[] TTL eviction (no more 256-cap wedge). L3 FirstBoot checks the
  chpass result (no more false success). L2 FirstBoot sets the credential via
  POST (password out of the URL) with a GET fallback so it cannot regress the
  v1.6.6c lockout. L5 self_heal throttled to every 3rd poll. §4 self_heal now
  probes GKI/GKN/ip6tables too. I1 gkd reloads seen.tsv on start (no duplicate
  new-device logs across a self-restart). I2 rtrafd class poll 2s->4s.
